    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm working on some schema design and i'm currently at 2nf. can u walk me through the steps to get it to 3nf? i'm trying to figure out how to handle the transitive dependencies so we don't end up with a bunch of redundant info in the tables.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To move from 2NF to 3NF, you need to eliminate all transitive dependencies. A transitive dependency exists when a non-key attribute is dependent on another non-key attribute, rather than directly on the primary key. Simply put, if $A \\rightarrow B$ and $B \\rightarrow C$, but $A$ is the primary key, then $C$ transitively depends on $A$ through $B$. You resolve this by creating a new table for the attributes involved in the transitive dependency.",
      "source": "target",
